    "message": {
      "content": "# Validation Checklist: Multi-Node Language-Model Serving System\n\n## Scope and Preconditions\n\nBefore any validation run, establish:\n\n- [ ] **System topology documented**: number of nodes, GPUs/accelerators per node, interconnect (InfiniBand/RoCE/NVLink/PCIe), scheduler (Slurm/K8s/MPI/torchrun), and serving framework version (vLLM, TensorRT-LLM, DeepSpeed-MII, custom).\n- [ ] **Baseline definition agreed**: what \"correct\" means for this system \u2014 identical outputs to single-node reference, statistical equivalence, or throughput/latency SLOs.\n- [ ] **Test environment frozen**: driver versions, CUDA/ROCm versions, NCCL/Gloo versions, container images (digest hashes, not tags), and model weights (checksummed).\n- [ ] **Validation runs executed by someone other than the system author where feasible**, or at minimum reviewed by a second engineer.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Configuration Identity\n\n**Goal: prove that all nodes are running the same logical system.**\n\n- [ ] **Model identity**: all nodes load weights from the same source with verified checksums (SHA-256 of safetensors/bin files). Record tokenizer version and any quantization config.\n- [ ] **Config hash propagation**: compute a hash of the full serving config (model path, dtype, tensor-parallel size, pipeline-parallel size, max batch size, max sequence length, KV-cache settings, sampling defaults) and verify every rank logs the identical hash at startup.\n- [ ] **Environment parity**: compare `nvidia-smi -q` output, NCCL version, and relevant env vars (`NCCL_DEBUG`, `NCCL_IB_HCA`, `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES`, `OMP_NUM_THREADS`) across all nodes. Divergence here is a common silent failure source.\n- [ ] **Code version pinning**: all nodes run the same commit hash / container digest",
      "reasoning": "",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
